{
  "id": "visceral-learning",
  "term": "visceral learning",
  "definition": "Visceral learning is aversive learning in which internal bodily pain, such as rectal pain, acts as the unconditioned stimulus so that previously neutral cues come to predict and acquire unpleasant meaning. It also includes related memory processes such as extinction of the learned response and possible reactivation of the earlier pain-associated memory trace.",
